    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_3d869ead",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the teacher as a representative of 'a good american'",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the teacher (visual material) through the textual overlay 'a good american' positioned above him. This creates an implicit identification where the viewer sees themselves or their societal role reflected in the teacher's figure, who is symbolically equated with the idealized 'good american'. The projection is not explicit (e.g., no 'you' or 'me'), but it is implied through the direct textual mapping and the viewer's role as an observer of the scene, making the teacher a stand-in for the user's potential self-identification with the concept of 'good american'.",
